## Explanation

- **More restarts (40 → 60)**: more randomized greedy seeds give the local search more diverse basins to escape poor local optima, at negligible runtime cost (execution time was only ~0.04s).
- **Iterated local search polish**: after the multi-start phase, the best placement is perturbed (a few random feasible relocations) and re-optimized via the existing lexicographic local search. This exploits the current structure and typically finds further max-KVPR reductions that pure restarts miss.
- **`rebuild`/`max_kvpr_of` helpers** deduplicate state recomputation, slightly simplifying the code while keeping the exact same objective and feasibility constraints (all placements respect `GPU_MEM_SIZE`).
